+The CLI shutdown test sends SIGTERM directly with the test-only `rustix`
+process wrapper. It needs no `/bin/kill` utility, which is absent from the
+minimal Debian 12 CI container. It still waits for the real service diagnostic
+before signaling, then requires successful exit, finished recording, no dropped
+rows and release of the service owner. Production dependencies, signal handling
+and timing are unchanged. The portability failure and subsequent checks are
+recorded in Third's log; CI evidence is distinct from lamp qualification.
